WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.899
In the late '90s, Sarah Michelle Gellar was
in command of both the big and small screens,

00:00:04.899 --> 00:00:08.680
but nowadays she seems to have been relegated
to the world of TV animation voice-overs.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.940
Here's a look at why Hollywood won't cast
Sarah Michelle Gellar anymore.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.200
Frightcasting

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.329
Gellar might have gotten her start on the
soap operas Swans Crossing and All My Children,

00:00:18.329 --> 00:00:20.970
but she really made her name as a scream queen.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:25.340
Just as she stepped into the title role in
TV's Buffy the Vampire Slayer, she also appeared

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:30.720
in the 1997 cheesetastic teen thrillers I
Know What You Did Last Summer and Scream 2.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.720
"Aaahh!

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.140
Please No!

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.620
Stooooppppppp!"

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.160
Almost all of her silver screen successes
since then can neatly fit into that same horror

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:45.370
box, like 2004's The Grudge, its 2006 sequel,
and The Return from the same year.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.510
Even her family film work in the live-action
Scooby-Doo flicks only boosted her scary movie

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.570
reputation — a reputation she now can't
escape.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:54.310
"Now who's the damsel in distress?"

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:54.980
"Me?"

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.100
"Straight up"

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.020
"Aaahhhh!"

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:02.240
Bad box office

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:07.130
Gellar gained instant popularity thanks to
Buffy and her fun slasher fare, but her efforts

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:09.510
outside the fear sphere have failed to lift
off.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:14.680
Her supernatural rom-com Simply Irresistible
was a flat-out flop, and nobody saw her weird

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.240
crime drama Harvard Man.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.420
No one saw her part as a viral porn star in
the dramedy Southland Tales, either.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.840
Or her psychological drama Veronika Decides
to Die.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.420
She's proven she can put bottoms in seats
whenever someone's chasing her with a knife,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.979
but viewers just haven't shown up to check
out her other offerings.

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:32.390
Killed by critics

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.630
Gellar's movies have received almost universal
disapproval from reviewers — even those

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.080
few films audiences did come out for.

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:44.220
Simply Irresistible, for instance, earned
an embarrassing 13% rating on Rotten Tomatoes,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:47.729
and The Return was massacred, too, earning
just 16%.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:51.830
Even The Grudge was mostly disliked, and the
sequel was a magnet for critical thrashing.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:02:00.700
When you look at that resume, it almost starts
to look like career suicide.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.150
Small screen struggles

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:06.670
Buffy was a fan-frenzied highlight of Gellar's
career, so once her movie star status proved

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:11.790
to be DOA, she returned to TV to see if she
might be able to find favor with at-home audiences

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.790
again.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.090
And she got her answer: nope.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:18.900
Her crime drama Ringer, which featured Gellar
as a pair of twins on the run from scary ne'er-do-wells,

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.480
bombed with critics and audiences alike, and
failed to earn a second season.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.760
Then her network comedy show The Crazy Ones,
which featured her alongside the late great

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.069
Robin Williams, also got the axe after a single
season.

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:32.069
Ouch.

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:33.150
Low profile

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.380
Her off-screen exploits haven't done much
to boost her profile either.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.980
Her long-lived marriage to fellow '90s hottie
Freddie Prinze Jr. has produced two children

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:41.980
and zero drama.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.760
Meanwhile, her social media feed oozes with
total proud mom gush, like a zillion pics

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.960
of her kids, and snaps of her family's culinary
adventures.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.069
It's all fantastic for her personal well-being,
but that kind of wild and crazy life doesn't

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:55.650
exactly keep up in the headlines.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.250
"Would you like to smoke a bowl?"

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.320
"Ya there's nothing in it."

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.900
Vocal victory

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.890
She's got a face for the cameras, no doubt.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:12.300
But post-Buffy, Gellar's had better responses
to her voice work than her screen appearances.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.239
She's done almost a decade's worth of audio
character work for Cartoon Network's Robot

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:20.989
Chicken, and you've heard her other places,
too, like The Simpsons,TMNT, and even video

00:03:20.989 --> 00:03:22.470
games like Call of Duty.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.380
"Let's puree some zombies!"

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.330
Most recently, she and Prinze have tapped
into the nerd domain with their voice roles

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:32.959
in Star Wars Rebels and seem to be drumming
up some solid fanfare as a result of that

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:33.959
show.

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:34.959
It's not over yet

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:39.050
One thing that could turn this all around
is if the Cruel Intentions TV sequel finally

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.459
takes flight.

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:44.070
Audiences nostalgic for Kathryn's special
kind of deviance might respond, if and when

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.209
the show is ever made.

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:48.109
"I'll give you something you've been obsessing
about."

00:03:48.109 --> 00:03:52.680
It wasn't mentioned on the fall 2016 order
sheets for any networks, but Gellar said the

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.680
delays were only due to the fact that they
want to get it right.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.680
"The road is taking a little longer than normal,
but we've all been adamite that to do it,

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.270
we have to do it right.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:05.690
And we have to do it, y'know, it's a naughty
show.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:10.040
And you have to pay homage to what it is and
you have to make sure that it all fits."

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.430
Let's hope they do.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.430
Thanks for watching!

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.300
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.959
And leave us a comment to let us know what
kind of roles you'd like to see Sarah Michelle

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:20.239
Gellar take on next…

